Derive the second plane of a single-buffer P010 capture format.

V4L2 P010 is one buffer with two color planes, the same shape as NV12 with
16-bit samples. Chromium only invented the chroma plane for NV12, so a P010
buffer never became a frame and 10-bit VP9 stayed at time 0. The chroma
plane now uses the same stride and half the height. bytesperline is already
in bytes. Any stateless driver that exports P010 as one plane needs this.
It is not specific to Apple.

--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc	2026-11-18 13:37:58.529859101 -0300
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc	2026-11-18 13:39:17.369585452 -0300
@@ -278,8 +278,9 @@
     const size_t y_stride_abs = static_cast<size_t>(y_stride);
     switch (pix_fmt) {
       case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12:
-        // The stride of UV is the same as Y in NV12.
-        // The height is half of Y plane.
+      case V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010:
+        // UV has the same stride as Y and half the height. P010 is the
+        // 16-bit version of that layout; bytesperline is already in bytes.
         planes.emplace_back(y_stride, y_stride_abs * pix_mp.height,
                             y_stride_abs * pix_mp.height / 2);
         DCHECK_EQ(2u, planes.size());
